🚀 Day 6 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 88 – Merge Sorted Array.

This problem reinforced my understanding of the Two Pointers technique and how to merge two sorted arrays efficiently without using any extra space.

💡 Approach: Two Pointers (Back-to-Front Merge)

Instead of creating a new array, I started comparing elements from the end of both arrays. Since nums1 already has enough extra space, I placed the larger element at the last available position and moved the corresponding pointer. After one array was exhausted, I copied the remaining elements from nums2 into nums1.

This approach avoids unnecessary shifting of elements and achieves an efficient in-place merge.

📚 Key Learnings:
✅ Mastering the Two Pointers technique
✅ Performing in-place merging without extra memory
✅ Utilizing the unused space in nums1 effectively
✅ Avoiding unnecessary element shifting
✅ Achieving an optimized O(m + n) time complexity with O(1) extra space

